# Functional collection prototype

Input: `product/product.yaml`. Product rationale, flows and supplied references:
`product/PRODUCT.md`. The Harness generated this example without calling a model.
The project does not depend on the Harness at runtime.

```bash
make up
# Open http://127.0.0.1:5173
make test
make lint
```

Routes: `#/` lists and filters the collection, `#/new` creates an item, and
`#/items/<id>` loads its detail. Refresh and browser back work on these hash routes.
The frontend talks to a real API through the Vite same-origin proxy. It does not
pretend a write succeeded or fall back to fixtures when the API is unavailable.

Contract: `GET /api/items`, `GET /api/items/{id}`, `POST /api/items` with title,
description and a declared status. FastAPI publishes OpenAPI at `/api/openapi.json`
and interactive docs at `/api/docs`. Responses use 201 plus Location for creation,
404 for missing items, 422 for invalid payloads, 409 when the memory limit is reached.
Domain and use cases use repository ports; the in-memory adapter is replaceable.

Browser E2E against the running web/API (Node 24 required on the host):

```bash
cd apps/web
npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund
PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH="$PWD/.playwright" npx --no-install playwright install chromium
PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH="$PWD/.playwright" npm run test:e2e
```

Set `E2E_BASE_URL` if using another local port. Tests run Chromium desktop and mobile
emulation, with real create/list/detail requests, reload/back, filtering, input
validation, missing-record and simulated network-failure recovery. Browser tests
add synthetic records; restart the API to return to initial seeds. Screenshots and
traces of failures appear in `apps/web/test-results`; HTML report in `playwright-report`.

This renderer supports exactly one entity with `title`, `description`, `status` and
list/detail/create screens. It rejects unsupported entities, screens and external/AI
integrations. Free-text constraints and visual directions are preserved for human/host
review, not automatically implemented. Only product content, status choices and the
accent color are applied deterministically. References are copied to documentation,
not embedded into the UI or interpreted by the generator.

Local prototype only: no login, public deployment, durable storage, update/delete,
attachments or AI. Up to 1000 items live in one API process; they survive browser
reload but reset on API restart and are not shared between workers. Use synthetic
data only. Compose binds host ports to loopback. Request schemas reject unknown
fields and bound text lengths. No credentials belong in this prototype.

The default visual layout uses English UI labels and system fonts; product content
can be supplied in another language, but the renderer does not localize all UI text.
Use `skills/project-design/SKILL.md` in a capable host to continue design work.
This file is provided for explicit use; no global skill installation occurs.
OpenSpec retains ownership of change workflows; Agent OS retains standards.
